[''Public'', ''Private'']', '[''STEM'', ''Engineering'', ''IT'', ''Education'', ''Medical'', ''Business'', ''Agriculture'', ''Arts'']', '[''All standard tracks'']', 'Filipino', 120000, 75.0, NULL, NULL, 'LGU', 'Need', '[''IP'']', '[]', '[]', FALSE, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 8000, '[''BARANGAY_CERT'', ''TOR'', ''ITR'']', FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, '2026-08-31', '2026-07-01', '2026-2027', TRUE, NULL, '[]', 'gemini_research', '2025-07-05', '2025-09-02', 'semester', NULL, 'csv_import', 0.81, 'needs_review', 'broken', '2026-08-02 21:44:54.998663', 34, NULL, 'e9daa7633e8f5444bcb22b3bcf55bbb597bce49b5239c39e281c407e41f826d5', FALSE, 'https://ykrinwegrgabjaltbbwz.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/scholarship-images/51/28b65c5f.webp', 'Tabuk City College Academic Scholarship', 'needs_verification', 81, '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', 'exact', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'scholarship', NULL, 58, 'needs_review');
INSERT INTO "scholarships" (id, title, provider, link, description, countries, regions, eligible_levels, eligible_regions, eligible_cities, residency_required, eligible_school_types, eligible_courses_psced, eligible_courses_specific, citizenship_required, max_income_threshold, min_gwa_normalized, min_age, max_age, provider_type, scholarship_type, priority_groups, preferred_extracurriculars, preferred_awards, benefit_tuition, benefit_allowance_monthly, benefit_books, benefit_miscellaneous, benefit_total_value, required_documents, has_qualifying_exam, has_interview, has_essay_requirement, has_return_service, application_deadline, application_open_date, academic_year_target, is_active, level, needs_tags, source, last_open_date, last_close_date, cycle_type, last_verified_at, verification_source, confidence_score, data_status, link_status, link_last_checked_at, link_failure_count, sponsor_id, dedupe_key, members_only, image_url, image_alt, application_status, data_completeness_score, eligible_schools, eligible_school_systems, eligible_school_categories, eligible_year_levels, eligible_enrollment_status, deadline_precision, deadline_note, deadline_source_url, verified_by, next_review_date, opportunity_type, type_attributes, organization_id, editorial_state) VALUES (52, 'NCIP Educational Assistance Program Degree Track', 'National Commission on Indigenous Peoples', 'https://ncip.gov.ph', 'The National Commission on Indigenous Peoples Educational Assistance Program (NCIP-EAP) Degree Track is a mandated sector-specific government program designed under NCIP Administrative Order No. 5 Series of 2012 and upgraded via AO No. 6 Series of 2023. It aims to extend tertiary educational access to recognized members of Indigenous Cultural Communities (ICCs/IPs) nationwide. Eligible candidates must secure a Certificate of Confirmation (COCO) from the NCIP Provincial/Regional Office confirming tribal identity. The academic bar requires a general passing GWA of 75% with zero dropped modules. It supplies an annual educational subsidy of 10,000 PHP to 20,000 PHP disbursed through regional offices to offset books, uniform, and field research. Highly recurring cycle synchronized with the fiscal year.', '', '', '[''College'']', '[]', '[]', TRUE, '[''Public'', ''Private'']', '[''STEM'', ''Engineering'', ''IT'', ''Education'', ''Medical'', ''Business'', ''Agriculture'', ''Arts'']', '[''All undergraduate pathways'']', 'Filipino', 200000, 75.0, NULL, NULL, 'Government', 'Need', '[''IP'']', '[]', '[]', FALSE, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 20000, '[''BARANGAY_CERT'', ''BIRTH_CERT'', ''TOR'']', FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, '2026-08-15', '2026-06-01', '2026-2027', TRUE, NULL, '[]', 'gemini_research', '2025-06-10', '2025-08-20', 'annual', '2026-06-30 12:31:14.487683', 'manual', 0.83, 'needs_review', 'broken', '2026-08-02 21:42:50.726635', 34, NULL, '6b673e1321dd9e2b746b6b254f4e28d0b0a151cbae227429560e1bbae7408842', FALSE, 'https://ykrinwegrgabjaltbbwz.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/scholarship-images/52/355de0af.webp', 'NCIP Educational Assistance Program Degree Track', 'needs_verification', 83, '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', 'exact', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'scholarship', NULL, 35, 'needs_review');
INSERT INTO "scholarships" (id, title, provider, link, description, countries, regions, eligible_levels, eligible_regions, eligible_cities, residency_required, eligible_school_types, eligible_courses_psced, eligible_courses_specific, citizenship_required, max_income_threshold, min_gwa_normalized, min_age, max_age, provider_type, scholarship_type, priority_groups, preferred_extracurriculars, preferred_awards, benefit_tuition, benefit_allowance_monthly, benefit_books, benefit_miscellaneous, benefit_total_value, required_documents, has_qualifying_exam, has_interview, has_essay_requirement, has_return_service, application_deadline, application_open_date, academic_year_target, is_active, level, needs_tags, source, last_open_date, last_close_date, cycle_type, last_verified_at, verification_source, confidence_score, data_status, link_status, link_last_checked_at, link_failure_count, sponsor_id, dedupe_key, members_only, image_url, image_alt, application_status, data_completeness_score, eligible_schools, eligible_school_systems, eligible_school_categories, eligible_year_levels, eligible_enrollment_status, deadline_precision, deadline_note, deadline_source_url, verified_by, next_review_date, opportunity_type, type_attributes, organization_id, editorial_state) VALUES (53, 'NCIP Merit Based Scholarship Program', 'National Commission on Indigenous Peoples', 'https://ncip.gov.ph', 'The NCIP Merit-Based Scholarship Program (NCIP-MBS) is a high-tier academic track within the commission reserved for outstanding IP students pursuing competitive national degrees (specifically STEM, Engineering, or Agriculture). Unlike the EAP, the MBS enforces a strict GWA requirement of 85% or higher and puts applicants through a competitive regional examination. It grants an expanded benefit package of 30,000 PHP per year to handle tuition balances or modern learning devices. Administered via the NCIP Bureau of Socio-Economic Literacy and Culture.', '', '', '[''College'']', '[]', '[]', TRUE, '[''Public'', ''Private'']', '[''STEM'', ''Engineering'', ''Agriculture'']', '[''STEM and Agriculture tracks'']', 'Filipino', 300000, 85.0, NULL, NULL, 'Government', 'Merit-based', '[''IP'']', '[]', '[]', TRUE, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 30000, '[''BARANGAY_CERT'', ''TOR'', ''GOOD_MORAL'']', TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, '2026-08-15', '2026-06-01', '2026-2027', TRUE, NULL, '[]', 'gemini_research', '2025-06-10', '2025-08-20', 'annual', '2026-06-30 12:31:16.675804', 'manual', 0.83, 'needs_review', 'broken', '2026-08-02 21:43:14.057123', 34, NULL, 'e5a3468dc58214d83d8c06c770ba23053dd2798ebbfe57051771be654288a1f9', FALSE, 'https://ykrinwegrgabjaltbbwz.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/scholarship-images/53/355de0af.webp', 'NCIP Merit Based Scholarship Program', 'needs_verification', 83, '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', 'exact', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'scholarship', NULL, 35, 'needs_review');
INSERT INTO "scholarships" (id, title, provider, link, description, countries, regions, eligible_levels, eligible_regions, eligible_cities, residency_required, eligible_school_types, eligible_courses_psced, eligible_courses_specific, citizenship_required, max_income_threshold, min_gwa_normalized, min_age, max_age, provider_type, scholarship_type, priority_groups, preferred_extracurriculars, preferred_awards, benefit_tuition, benefit_allowance_monthly, benefit_books, benefit_miscellaneous, benefit_total_value, required_documents, has_qualifying_exam, has_interview, has_essay_requirement, has_return_service, application_deadline, application_open_date, academic_year_target, is_active, level, needs_tags, source, last_open_date, last_close_date, cycle_type, last_verified_at, verification_source, confidence_score, data_status, link_status, link_last_checked_at, link_failure_count, sponsor_id, dedupe_key, members_only, image_url, image_alt, application_status, data_completeness_score, eligible_schools, eligible_school_systems, eligible_school_categories, eligible_year_levels, eligible_enrollment_status, deadline_precision, deadline_note, deadline_source_url, verified_by, next_review_date, opportunity_type, type_attributes, organization_id, editorial_state) VALUES (54, 'CHED Medical Scholarship and Return Service (MSRS)', 'Commission on Higher Education', 'https://legacy.ched.gov.ph/msrs/', 'The DOH Medical Scholarship and Return Service (MSRS) Program is a major sector-specific government intervention operating under the ''Doktor Para sa Bayan'' Act (RA 11509) in partnership with CHED. It funds full medical education (Doctor of Medicine) for qualified Filipino students across certified state and partner private universities. It covers 100% of tuition, laboratory fees, provides a high monthly living allowance of 15,000 PHP, a specialized book/equipment allowance of 20,000 PHP per semester, and basic board exam review subsidies. Eligible applicants must hold a Bachelor''s degree with a solid GWA, pass the medical school entrance and NMAT, and prioritize low-income roots or origin from underserved rural towns. Return service requires serving as a public health officer in a government hospital or rural health unit (RHU) for 1 year for every year of scholarship.', '', '', '[''Graduate'']', '[]', '[]', FALSE, '[''Public'', ''Private'']', '[''Medical'']', '[''Doctor of Medicine (MD)'']', 'Filipino', 600000, 85.0, NULL, NULL, 'Government', 'Merit-and-Need', '[''Rural Public Health'']', '[]', '[]', TRUE, 15000, TRUE, NULL, 250000, '[''TOR'', ''BIRTH_CERT'', ''GOOD_MORAL'', ''ITR'', ''ESSAY'']', TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, NULL, NULL, '2026-2027', TRUE, NULL, '[]', 'gemini_research', '2025-05-15', '2026-06-30', 'annual', '2026-06-30 12:31:17.780959', 'manual', 0.13, 'needs_review', 'ok', '2026-08-02 21:44:30.682077', 0, NULL, '1bd7cebd8dd4aefe691eae0ddf4b73b809ef0a5cdf8a55d7d72de51a42cc0ef1', FALSE, 'https://ykrinwegrgabjaltbbwz.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/scholarship-images/54/e98944a0.webp', 'DOH Medical Scholarship and Return Service Program', 'needs_verification', 13, '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', 'exact', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'scholarship', NULL, 7, 'needs_review');
INSERT INTO "scholarships" (id, title, provider, link, description, countries, regions, eligible_levels, eligible_regions, eligible_cities, residency_required, eligible_school_types, eligible_courses_psced, eligible_courses_specific, citizenship_required, max_income_threshold, min_gwa_normalized, min_age, max_age, provider_type, scholarship_type, priority_groups, preferred_extracurriculars, preferred_awards, benefit_tuition, benefit_allowance_monthly, benefit_books, benefit_miscellaneous, benefit_total_value, required_documents, has_qualifying_exam, has_interview, has_essay_requirement, has_return_service, application_deadline, application_open_date, academic_year_target, is_active, level, needs_tags, source, last_open_date, last_close_date, cycle_type, last_verified_at, verification_source, confidence_score, data_status, link_status, link_last_checked_at, link_failure_count, sponsor_id, dedupe_key, members_only, image_url, image_alt, application_status, data_completeness_score, eligible_schools, eligible_school_systems, eligible_school_categories, eligible_year_levels, eligible_enrollment_status, deadline_precision, deadline_note, deadline_source_url, verified_by, next_review_date, opportunity_type, type_attributes, organization_id, editorial_state) VALUES (55, 'Department of Agriculture ACEF GIAHEP SUC Track', 'Department of Agriculture', 'https://da.gov.ph', 'The Agricultural Competitiveness Enhancement Fund Grants-in-Aid for Higher Education Program (ACEF-GIAHEP) SUC Track is a targeted government financial aid tool managed by the Department of Agriculture in compliance with RA 10848. It extends funding to children of registered small farmers, fisherfolk, and agrarian reform beneficiaries who are enrolled in State Universities and Colleges. It covers educational assistance for specific courses in agriculture, agribusiness, agricultural engineering, and fisheries science. Requires a minimum GWA of 75% and presentation of the parent''s RSBSA (Registry System for Basic Sectors in Agriculture) certificate. Disburses a flat rate of 15,000 PHP per semester.', '', '', '[''College'']', '[]', '[]', FALSE, '[''Public'']', '[''Agriculture'', ''Engineering'']', '[''Agriculture and Agribusiness'']', 'Filipino', 200000, 75.0, NULL, NULL, 'Government', 'Need', '[''Farmer/Fisher Dependent'']', '[]', '[]', TRUE, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 30000, '[''BARANGAY_CERT'', ''TOR'', ''BIRTH_CERT'']', FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, '2026-08-15', '2026-06-15', '2026-2027', TRUE, NULL, '[]', 'gemini_research', '2025-06-20', '2025-08-25', 'annual', NULL, 'csv_import', 0.75, 'needs_review', 'ok', '2026-08-02 21:42:49.515458', 0, NULL, 'f8db6484aba09bf384c25d93d8e5e9b891fa3f037c24def1d9dd361816df5658', FALSE, 'https://ykrinwegrgabjaltbbwz.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/scholarship-images/55/e9afdebf.webp', 'Department of Agriculture ACEF GIAHEP SUC Track', 'needs_verification', 75, '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', 'exact', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'scholarship', NULL, 29, 'needs_review');
INSERT INTO "scholarships" (id, title, provider, link, description, countries, regions, eligible_levels, eligible_regions, eligible_cities, residency_required, eligible_school_types, eligible_courses_psced, eligible_courses_specific, citizenship_required, max_income_threshold, min_gwa_normalized, min_age, max_age, provider_type, scholarship_type, priority_groups, preferred_extracurriculars, preferred_awards, benefit_tuition, benefit_allowance_monthly, benefit_books, benefit_miscellaneous, benefit_total_value, required_documents, has_qualifying_exam, has_interview, has_essay_requirement, has_return_service, application_deadline, application_open_date, academic_year_target, is_active, level, needs_tags, source, last_open_date, last_close_date, cycle_type, last_verified_at, verification_source, confidence_score, data_status, link_status, link_last_checked_at, link_failure_count, sponsor_id, dedupe_key, members_only, image_url, image_alt, application_status, data_completeness_score, eligible_schools, eligible_school_systems, eligible_school_categories, eligible_year_levels, eligible_enrollment_status, deadline_precision, deadline_note, deadline_source_url, verified_by, next_review_date, opportunity_type, type_attributes, organization_id, editorial_state) VALUES (56, 'AFPEBSO DND CHED PASUC Scholarship', 'Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFPEBSO)', 'https://afpeebso.org', 'The AFPEBSO DND-CHED-PASUC Scholarship is a special sector-specific inter-agency government program managed by the Armed Forces of the Philippines Educational Benefit System Office. It extends 100% tuition and fee exemptions at any public State University or College (SUC) for the legitimate children and direct dependents of active-duty, retired, or deceased AFP military personnel. Academic requirements mandate a baseline GWA of 80% (2.5) with zero failures. Financial constraints are secondary to the parent''s military service record. Portals accept applications annually from May to July.', '', '', '[''College'']', '[]', '[]', TRUE, '[''Public'']', '[''STEM'', ''Engineering'', ''IT'', ''Education'', ''Medical'', ''Business'', ''Agriculture'', ''Arts'']', '[''All SUC undergraduate paths'']', 'Filipino', NULL, 80.0, NULL, NULL, 'Government', 'Affiliation', '[''Military Dependents'']', '[]', '[]', TRUE, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 15000, '[''BARANGAY_CERT'', ''TOR'', ''BIRTH_CERT'']', FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-2027', TRUE, NULL, '[]', 'gemini_research', '2025-05-10', '2026-07-15', 'annual', '2026-06-30 12:31:21.146367', 'manual', 0.68, 'needs_review', 'broken', '2026-08-02 21:42:58.072872', 34, NULL, '1fac5d3a42b6f56b9cd5290516c9ea744e640280900d1e056934a1871c4a3909', TRUE, 'https://ykrinwegrgabjaltbbwz.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/scholarship-images/56/13964d5e.webp', 'AFPEBSO DND CHED PASUC Scholarship', 'needs_verification', 68, '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', 'exact', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'scholarship', NULL, 14, 'needs_review');
INSERT INTO "scholarships" (id, title, provider, link, description, countries, regions, eligible_levels, eligible_regions, eligible_cities, residency_required, eligible_school_types, eligible_courses_psced, eligible_courses_specific, citizenship_required, max_income_threshold, min_gwa_normalized, min_age, max_age, provider_type, scholarship_type, priority_groups, preferred_extracurriculars, preferred_awards, benefit_tuition, benefit_allowance_monthly, benefit_books, benefit_miscellaneous, benefit_total_value, required_documents, has_qualifying_exam, has_interview, has_essay_requirement, has_return_service, application_deadline, application_open_date, academic_year_target, is_active, level, needs_tags, source, last_open_date, last_close_date, cycle_type, last_verified_at, verification_source, confidence_score, data_status, link_status, link_last_checked_at, link_failure_count, sponsor_id, dedupe_key, members_only, image_url, image_alt, application_status, data_completeness_score, eligible_schools, eligible_school_systems, eligible_school_categories, eligible_year_levels, eligible_enrollment_status, deadline_precision, deadline_note, deadline_source_url, verified_by, next_review_date, opportunity_type, type_attributes, organization_id, editorial_state) VALUES (57, 'DSWD AICS Educational Assistance', 'Department of Social Welfare and Development', 'https://www.dswd.gov.ph', 'The DSWD Assistance to Individuals in Crisis Situation (AICS) Educational Assistance is a specialized cash intervention program designed for students experiencing extreme economic shock, sudden death of a breadwinner, abandonment, or loss of livelihood due to national disasters. Operated directly through the DSWD Crisis Intervention Units (CIU) or Social Welfare Operations Hubs, it provides a one-time cash grant ranging from 1,000 PHP (Elementary), 2,000 PHP (High School), 3,000 PHP (Senior High), to 4,000 PHP (College/TVET) per semester. Selection ignores GWA rankings but strictly requires an active Case Study Report or Certificate of Indigency from the local MSWDO.', '', '', '[''Grade 11'', ''Grade 12'', ''College'', ''TVET'', ''Graduate'']', '[]', '[]', FALSE, '[''Public'', ''Private'']', '[''STEM'', ''Engineering'', ''IT'', ''Education'', ''Medical'', ''Business'', ''Agriculture'', ''Arts'']', '[''All educational lines'']', 'Filipino', 150000, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Government', 'Need', '[''Students in Crisis'']', '[]', '[]', FALSE, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 4000, '[''BARANGAY_CERT'', ''BIRTH_CERT'', ''4PS_CERT'', ''TOR'']', FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, '2026-12-31', '2026-01-01', '2026-2027', TRUE, NULL, '[]', 'gemini_research', '2025-01-05', '2025-12-28', 'rolling', '2026-06-30 12:31:22.946738', 'manual', 0.83, 'needs_review', 'timeout', '2026-08-02 21:45:06.760466', 1, NULL, 'f367035dae8c99de0abdb2705231d07c4e7871305f1664dfc5a66fab431a8dba', FALSE, 'https://ykrinwegrgabjaltbbwz.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/scholarship-images/57/0bdab539.webp', 'DSWD AICS Educational Assistance', 'needs_verification', 83, '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', 'exact', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'scholarship', NULL, 52, 'needs_review');
INSERT INTO "scholarships" (id, title, provider, link, description, countries, regions, eligible_levels, eligible_regions, eligible_cities, residency_required, eligible_school_types, eligible_courses_psced, eligible_courses_specific, citizenship_required, max_income_threshold, min_gwa_normalized, min_age, max_age, provider_type, scholarship_type, priority_groups, preferred_extracurriculars, preferred_awards, benefit_tuition, benefit_allowance_monthly, benefit_books, benefit_miscellaneous, benefit_total_value, required_documents, has_qualifying_exam, has_interview, has_essay_requirement, has_return_service, application_deadline, application_open_date, academic_year_target, is_active, level, needs_tags, source, last_open_date, last_close_date, cycle_type, last_verified_at, verification_source, confidence_score, data_status, link_status, link_last_checked_at, link_failure_count, sponsor_id, dedupe_key, members_only, image_url, image_alt, application_status, data_completeness_score, eligible_schools, eligible_school_systems, eligible_school_categories, eligible_year_levels, eligible_enrollment_status, deadline_precision, deadline_note, deadline_source_url, verified_by, next_review_date, opportunity_type, type_attributes, organization_id, editorial_state) VALUES (58, 'Security Bank Foundation State Universities Scholarship', 'Security Bank Foundation', 'https://www.securitybank.com', 'The Security Bank Foundation ''Scholars for Better Communities'' State Universities Scholarship provides full educational stipends to low-income student leaders enrolled in partner public SUCs (such as UP Diliman, MSU, or regional centers). It provides a high flat allowance of 50,000 PHP per year to cover learning modules, laptops, and transit costs. Applicants must present a GWA of 85% or higher, zero failed subjects, and clear an interview with Security Bank HR personnel. No return service is mandated, but scholars receive priority onboarding for corporate internships.', '', '', '[''College'']', '[]', '[]', FALSE, '[''Public'']', '[''STEM'', ''Business'', ''IT'']', '[''Finance Accounting and IT courses'']', 'Filipino', 350000, 85.0, NULL, NULL, 'Private', 'Merit-and-Need', '[''Low Income Achievers'']', '[]', '[]', FALSE, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 50000, '[''TOR'', ''BIRTH_CERT'', ''GOOD_MORAL'', ''ITR'']', FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-2027', TRUE, NULL, '[]', 'gemini_research', '2025-04-20', '2026-06-15', 'annual', '2026-07-26 00:00:00', 'manual', 0.0, 'needs_review', 'broken', '2026-08-02 21:44:35.238057', 8, NULL, '26754cd9d7e4f7774caf78c79c91a6167d4a294e8bac5536e26e8251346281a2', FALSE, 'https://ykrinwegrgabjaltbbwz.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/scholarship-images/58/49d034ce.webp', 'Security Bank Foundation State Universities Scholarship', 'needs_verification', 0, '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', 'exact', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'scholarship', NULL, 19, 'needs_review');
INSERT INTO "scholarships" (id, title, provider, link, description, countries, regions, eligible_levels, eligible_regions, eligible_cities, residency_required, eligible_school_types, eligible_courses_psced, eligible_courses_specific, citizenship_required, max_income_threshold, min_gwa_normalized, min_age, max_age, provider_type, scholarship_type, priority_groups, preferred_extracurriculars, preferred_awards, benefit_tuition, benefit_allowance_monthly, benefit_books, benefit_miscellaneous, benefit_total_value, required_documents, has_qualifying_exam, has_interview, has_essay_requirement, has_return_service, application_deadline, application_open_date, academic_year_target, is_active, level, needs_tags, source, last_open_date, last_close_date, cycle_type, last_verified_at, verification_source, confidence_score, data_status, link_status, link_last_checked_at, link_failure_count, sponsor_id, dedupe_key, members_only, image_url, image_alt, application_status, data_completeness_score, eligible_schools, eligible_school_systems, eligible_school_categories, eligible_year_levels, eligible_enrollment_status, deadline_precision, deadline_note, deadline_source_url, verified_by, next_review_date, opportunity_type, type_attributes, organization_id, editorial_state) VALUES (59, 'Caritas Manila YSLEP Scholarship Program', 'Caritas Manila', 'https://www.caritasmanila.org.ph', 'The Youth Servant Leadership and Education Program (YSLEP) is Caritas Manila''s primary church-backed financial aid and leadership development initiative. Operating across Catholic dioceses nationwide, it supports poor and marginalized college and TVET students. It pays partial tuition up to 25,000 PHP per year and distributes a modest monthly allowance. Distinctively, selection prioritizes urban-slum families, 4Ps members, and indigenous youth. Recipients must join monthly leadership seminars, church volunteer hours, and community organizing programs. Academic criteria require a baseline 80% GWA with zero failures.', '', '', '[''College'', ''TVET'']', '[]', '[]', FALSE, '[''Public'', ''Private'']', '[''STEM'', ''Engineering'', ''IT'', ''Education'', ''Medical'', ''Business'', ''Agriculture'', ''Arts'']', '[''All approved courses'']', 'Filipino', 180000, 80.0, NULL, NULL, 'Private', 'Need', '[''4Ps/Listahanan'', ''Urban Slum Youth'']', '[]', '[]', TRUE, 1000, TRUE, NULL, 35000, '[''BARANGAY_CERT'', ''4PS_CERT'', ''TOR'', ''BIRTH_CERT'']', FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, NULL, NULL, '2026-2027', TRUE, NULL, '[]', 'gemini_research', '2025-05-10', '2026-07-15', 'annual', NULL, 'csv_import', 0.66, 'needs_review', 'ok', '2026-08-02 21:46:00.402248', 0, NULL, 'abbfd73a3ec90777d10142b12204027e003f9fe791f83ee9736fc91ef3d4b945', FALSE, 'https://ykrinwegrgabjaltbbwz.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/scholarship-images/59/9f7aa6ca.webp', 'Caritas Manila YSLEP Scholarship Program', 'needs_verification', 66, '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', 'exact', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'scholarship', NULL, 25, 'needs_review');
INSERT INTO "scholarships" (id, title, provider, link, description, countries, regions, eligible_levels, eligible_regions, eligible_cities, residency_required, eligible_school_types, eligible_courses_psced, eligible_courses_specific, citizenship_required, max_income_threshold, min_gwa_normalized, min_age, max_age, provider_type, scholarship_type, priority_groups, preferred_extracurriculars, preferred_awards, benefit_tuition, benefit_allowance_monthly, benefit_books, benefit_miscellaneous, benefit_total_value, required_documents, has_qualifying_exam, has_interview, has_essay_requirement, has_return_service, application_deadline, application_open_date, academic_year_target, is_active, level, needs_tags, source, last_open_date, last_close_date, cycle_type, last_verified_at, verification_source, confidence_score, data_status, link_status, link_last_checked_at, link_failure_count, sponsor_id, dedupe_key, members_only, image_url, image_alt, application_status, data_completeness_score, eligible_schools, eligible_school_systems, eligible_school_categories, eligible_year_levels, eligible_enrollment_status, deadline_precision, deadline_note, deadline_source_url, verified_by, next_review_date, opportunity_type, type_attributes, organization_id, editorial_state) VALUES (60, 'Taiwan ICDF Higher Education Scholarship Program', 'Taiwan International Cooperation and Development Fund', 'https://www.icdf.org.tw', 'The Taiwan ICDF Higher Education Scholarship Program is a full international bilateral grant offered to Filipino citizens for Master''s or Doctoral programs at partner Taiwanese universities. It provides full tuition coverage, modern campus housing, comprehensive health insurance, and a monthly stipend of 18,000 TWD (Master''s) or 20,000 TWD (PhD) (approximately 32,000 to 36,000 PHP). Focus areas are restricted to STEM, tropical agriculture, and electronic engineering. Requires an undergraduate GWA of 85% or better and an interview by the Taipei Economic and Cultural Office (TECO) in Manila.', '', '', '[''Graduate'']', '[]', '[]', FALSE, '[''Public'', ''Private'']', '[''STEM'', ''Engineering'', ''Agriculture'']', '[''STEM and Tropical Agriculture fields'']', 'Filipino', NULL, 85.0, NULL, NULL, 'Government', 'Merit-based', '[''Advanced Tech Researchers'']', '[]', '[]', TRUE, 35000, TRUE, NULL, 900000, '[''TOR'', ''BIRTH_CERT'', ''GOOD_MORAL'', ''ESSAY'']', FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-2027', TRUE, NULL, '[]', 'gemini_research', '2025-01-05', '2026-03-15', 'annual', '2026-07-26 00:00:00', 'manual', 0.0, 'needs_review', 'ok', '2026-08-02 21:42:20.862325', 0, NULL, '2e437df68438629c31bbb10fe3ca30242d228a95586eaa59c0d4364a61c2881a', FALSE, 'https://ykrinwegrgabjaltbbwz.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/scholarship-images/60/e1c0c369.webp', 'Taiwan ICDF Higher Education Scholarship Program', 'needs_verification', 0, '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', 'exact', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'scholarship', NULL, 27, 'needs_review');
INSERT INTO "scholarships" (id, title, provider, link, description, countries, regions, eligible_levels, eligible_regions, eligible_cities, residency_required, eligible_school_types, eligible_courses_psced, eligible_courses_specific, citizenship_required, max_income_threshold, min_gwa_normalized, min_age, max_age, provider_type, scholarship_type, priority_groups, preferred_extracurriculars, preferred_awards, benefit_tuition, benefit_allowance_monthly, benefit_books, benefit_miscellaneous, benefit_total_value, required_documents, has_qualifying_exam, has_interview, has_essay_requirement, has_return_service, application_deadline, application_open_date, academic_year_target, is_active, level, needs_tags, source, last_open_date, last_close_date, cycle_type, last_verified_at, verification_source, confidence_score, data_status, link_status, link_last_checked_at, link_failure_count, sponsor_id, dedupe_key, members_only, image_url, image_alt, application_status, data_completeness_score, eligible_schools, eligible_school_systems, eligible_school_categories, eligible_year_levels, eligible_enrollment_status, deadline_precision, deadline_note, deadline_source_url, verified_by, next_review_date, opportunity_type, type_attributes, organization_id, editorial_state) VALUES (61, 'Megaworld Foundation Scholarship Program', 'Megaworld Foundation', 'https://www.megaworldfoundation.com', 'The Megaworld Foundation Scholarship Program is a high-impact mid-market corporate financial assistance framework that funds full undergraduate degrees for underprivileged youths across partner universities in Metro Manila and key regions. It covers 100% of actual tuition and institutional fees, and issues a monthly stipend of 2,500 PHP. Eligible candidates must maintain a GWA of 85% (2.0) with zero dropped subjects and possess a total combined annual household income not exceeding 400,000 PHP. Applications are routed through the Megaworld online portal, requiring an essay on community development and an executive interview.', '', '', '[''College'']', '[''NCR'', ''Region III - Central Luzon'', ''Region IV-A - Calabarzon'', ''Region VI - Western Visayas'', ''Region VII - Central Visayas'']', '[]', FALSE, '[''Public'', ''Private'']', '[''STEM'', ''Engineering'', ''IT'', ''Business'', ''Arts'']', '[''Engineering Architecture and Tech'']', 'Filipino', 400000, 85.0, NULL, NULL, 'Private', 'Merit-and-Need', '[''Underprivileged Youth'']', '[]', '[]', TRUE, 2500, FALSE, NULL, 120000, '[''ITR'', ''BARANGAY_CERT'', ''TOR'', ''ESSAY'']', FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-2027', TRUE, NULL, '[]', 'gemini_research', '2025-05-20', '2026-07-15', 'annual', '2026-06-30 12:31:37.007309', 'manual', 0.36, 'needs_review', 'ok', '2026-08-02 21:44:39.130506', 0, NULL, 'a68a9d63f6e17c135201f20c13d8a091b592f6634d2cf28657c11b7a0b724b32', FALSE, 'https://ykrinwegrgabjaltbbwz.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/scholarship-images/61/fc437fa7.webp', 'Megaworld Foundation Scholarship Program', 'needs_verification', 36, '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', 'exact', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'scholarship', NULL, 31, 'needs_review');
INSERT INTO "scholarships" (id, title, provider, link, description, countries, regions, eligible_levels, eligible_regions, eligible_cities, residency_required, eligible_school_types, eligible_courses_psced, eligible_courses_specific, citizenship_required, max_income_threshold, min_gwa_normalized, min_age, max_age, provider_type, scholarship_type, priority_groups, preferred_extracurriculars, preferred_awards, benefit_tuition, benefit_allowance_monthly, benefit_books, benefit_miscellaneous, benefit_total_value, required_documents, has_qualifying_exam, has_interview, has_essay_requirement, has_return_service, application_deadline, application_open_date, academic_year_target, is_active, level, needs_tags, source, last_open_date, last_close_date, cycle_type, last_verified_at, verification_source, confidence_score, data_status, link_status, link_last_checked_at, link_failure_count, sponsor_id, dedupe_key, members_only, image_url, image_alt, application_status, data_completeness_score, eligible_schools, eligible_school_systems, eligible_school_categories, eligible_year_levels, eligible_enrollment_status, deadline_precision, deadline_note, deadline_source_url, verified_by, next_review_date, opportunity_type, type_attributes, organization_id, editorial_state) VALUES (62, 'AFPSLAI Educational Grant Program', 'Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFPSLAI)', 'https://www.afpslai.com.ph', 'The AFPSLAI Educational Grant Program (EGP) is an affiliation-based financial assistance platform run by the Armed Forces and Police Savings and Loan Association, Inc. It caters to the children and dependents of active or retired military personnel, PNP officers, and uniformed service members who are registered members of AFPSLAI. It delivers a comprehensive flat financial subsidy of 25,000 PHP per semester (50,000 PHP annually) directly to the student to offset undergraduate expenses. Candidates must post a minimum GWA of 85% and possess a clean disciplinary record. Submissions clear through AFPSLAI regional branch hubs.', '', '', '[''College'']', '[]', '[]', FALSE, '[''Public'', ''Private'']', '[''STEM'', ''Engineering'', ''IT'', ''Education'', ''Medical'', ''Business'', ''Agriculture'', ''Arts'']', '[''All undergraduate tracks'']', 'Filipino', 500000, 85.0, NULL, NULL, 'Private', 'Affiliation', '[''Uniformed Service Dependents'']', '[]', '[]', FALSE, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 50000, '[''TOR'', ''BIRTH_CERT'', ''GOOD_MORAL'']', FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-2027', TRUE, NULL, '[]', 'gemini_research', '2025-05-20', '2026-07-10', 'annual', NULL, 'csv_import', 0.66, 'needs_review', 'ok', '2026-08-02 21:43:04.065860', 0, NULL, '2d13eae2aa27892dcee03c7b4e869c7f89b42c13119201a7c14136921db5d517', TRUE, 'https://ykrinwegrgabjaltbbwz.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/scholarship-images/62/13964d5e.webp', 'AFPSLAI Educational Grant Program', 'needs_verification', 66, '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', 'exact', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'scholarship', NULL, 51, 'needs_review');
